iner Ship In Black Sea"}],"revisions":[{"revision":1,"changed_at":"2026-10-28T18:57:12Z"}],"entities":[{"name":"Black Sea","kind":"place","mentions":8},{"name":"Bulgaria","kind":"place","mentions":8},{"name":"Black Sea Near Bulgarian Coast","kind":"place","mentions":1},{"name":"Crew Safe","kind":"place","mentions":1},{"name":"Liberian","kind":"group","mentions":1},{"name":"Ship Struck","kind":"person","mentions":1},{"name":"Three Naval Drones","kind":"organisation","mentions":1},{"name":"the Black Sea","kind":"place","mentions":1}],"disputes":[],"summary":{"text":"A container ship in the Black Sea near Bulgaria was hit by three naval drones. The attack occurred on October 28, 2026, and the crew was safe and ashore. The incident happened in the Bulgarian Black Sea economic zone, and it is the fifth such attack in the area.","text_hi":null,"model":"qwen2.5-1.5b-instruct-q4_k_m.gguf","created_at":"2026-10-29T17:03:00Z"},"context":{"background":[],"places":[{"title":"Bulgaria","extract":"Bulgaria, officially the Republic of Bulgaria, is a country in Southeastern Europe. It is situated on the eastern portion of the Balkans directly south of the Danube river and west of the Black Sea. Bulgaria is bordered by Greece and Turkey to the south, Serbia and North Macedonia to the west, and Romania across the Danube river to the north. It covers a territory of 110,994 square kilometres (42,855 sq mi), making it the tenth largest within the European Union and the sixteenth-largest country in Europe by area. Sofia is the nation's capital and largest city; other major cities include Plovdiv, Varna, and Burgas.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Bulgaria","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"BG"},{"title":"Greece","extract":"Greece, officially the Hellenic Republic, is a country located mostly on the Balkan peninsula of Southeastern Europe, with thousands of islands extending geographically to Asia Minor. It has a population of around 10 million. With nine regions and up to 227 inhabited islands, it has the longest coastline on the Mediterranean. The Ionian Sea is west of the mainland, Albania northwest, and North Macedonia and Bulgaria north. Turkey is east both by land and the Aegean Sea. The capital, Athens, is the largest Greek city, followed by Thessaloniki and Patras.","url":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Greece","source":"Wikipedia","license":"CC BY-SA 4.0","iso2":"GR"}],"arc":{"reports":72,"first_seen":"2026-10-12T08:12:29Z","first_title":"Bulgaria to Seek EU Action to Protect Black Sea Shipping","first_url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMingFBVV95cUxPQWxlSUl2eldyRE9uX2R2VVRpX0RtcXdHY21nbm1vSzJrZU5mN0d5cWUzRHM4bVVGS25pUkdQcnEydHFTUTdnZHh2dGlRczV5OGV0UDZRdno3S1VHVk02Sk0zMGNZcUxQeUstUEdLSE05clphVGY0VjNoeENLM3ZZRDB3M3dwS0hQdnlyb3ZNU1h0bGRFWUJLQWZRcTNYZw?oc=5","first_publisher":"Novinite.com","earlier":[{"id":"e_3cb43dc0508d","title":"Bulgarian Navy Rescues 18 Seafarers After Drone Attack On Cargo Ship In Black Sea","date":"2026-10-29T13:14:33Z","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMisgFBVV95cUxNVU01MU9RNnYteS02bzJyZVRkbjZsNWRjbEFGWTZwTWVPNklsNF9xZ3g1S1NqZkFpR29MOURjSUZvNnNzTkczY1hzWmRfV0tQM3FjbWRiMUhfUG9KaDJ6X0ZYVTlyMWhjMS10a19xeFJCeHBRUHY4cTBHZWoxd283ZGxzQVhVbkgyME5JV05Nek5sUDZwd3NXUVpoMGgzSFBPaHRWQzVkZ1ZvNE1SdEhxd21n?oc=5","publisher":"Marine Insight","verification":"single_source_report"},{"id":"e_9d7707bf37b5","title":"Boat Drones Sink ZIM-Chartered Ship off Bulgaria, Crew Rescued","date":"2026-10-29T15:16:16Z","url":"https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMingFBVV95cUxQRnlMbTE4Ymp4SjFucTZsaW1HNVNvSGJJemxMQnpWbXFuWEtxVnBLZTE4eWg4ejlYUU8yMXFsZHlBU2thZU9fc0FZMHl6a0dvT0U4blpRaGVXZGdvdXVXTjZuVHViRDZxY25OZzlVX2w4V0R3cElUVzVFdzZxMjdmMGFndE4xOFUzbkVOSFkyMlBnY0g3ZG1xamluNjZHQQ?oc=5","publisher":"The Media Line","verification":"single_source_report"},{"id":"e_76b55c39807b","title":"Zim Confirms Loss of Containership Attacked in Black Sea off Bulgaria","date":"2026-10-29T17:04:39Z","url":"https://news.googl